# CLI Output and Color Conventions

All terminal output goes through `internal/output`. `internal/logging` is a thin shim over it (`logging.Info`, `Success`, `Warning`, `Error`, `Debug`, `Println`) so callers need no printer plumbing. There is no color library: `fatih/color` is gone and must not come back.

## Which call to use

| You are writing | Call | Stream (text mode) |
|---|---|---|
| A change was made or a check passed | `logging.Success` (`[ok]`) | stdout |
| Status, progress, no-op ("already configured") | `logging.Info` (`[info]`) | stdout |
| Something to look at, command went on | `logging.Warning` (`[warning]`) | stderr |
| A failure | return a `*CLIError`; `HandleError` prints `[error]` + action | stderr |
| Diagnostics for `--log-level debug` | `logging.Debug` (`[debug]`) | stderr |
| A labeled line to a writer that is not the process stream (tests, cobra `cmd.ErrOrStderr()`) | `writeLabeled(w, output.KindX, ...)` | w |
| A hint line / a notice | `writeAction` / `writeNotice` | w |
| Command data: tables, `key: value`, JSON, `true`/`false` | the `Renderer` (`rt.Out`) | stdout |
| Prompt context, menus, confirmation details | `writeProse` / `writePrompt` | w |
| A generated document (capella.yaml, guide text) | `writeDocument` | w |

Never call `fmt.Print*`, `fmt.Fprint*(os.Stdout|os.Stderr, ...)` or write raw `\x1b` codes in `internal/cli`. Writes to a `w` go through the helpers above so redaction and glyph rules apply. The only places allowed to touch the process streams are `internal/output` and the `Deps` defaults in `internal/cli/deps.go`. `cmd/cbdev` is a developer tool and keeps plain `fmt`.

Pick `[ok]` versus `[info]` by meaning: a message that says something was created, saved, removed, applied, imported or passed is `[ok]`; "already configured", "waiting for", "accepted", "Next:" are `[info]`. The stdout texts automation depends on do not change: `Cluster already configured`, `Node already configured`, `Collection not empty`, `Cluster created on ...`, `Imported N documents`, `Keyspace "..." created`.

## Format

```
[level] - message text
  -> action line (hint for the line above)
```

- Only the label word is styled. The brackets, the ` - ` and the message are **never** colored. The reset follows the closing bracket.
- Levels: `[ok]` (bold green `1;32`), `[info]` (plain), `[warning]` (bold yellow `1;33`), `[error]` (bold red `1;31`), `[debug]` (dim `2`).
- Escape codes are written by hand in `internal/output/label.go` (16-color SGR). Do not add a color library.
- Keep level names lowercase. A new level needs an entry in `internal/output/label.go`, a golden pair in `internal/output/testdata/golden`, and a row in the README label table.

## Streams

- `[ok]` and `[info]` go to stdout in text mode and to stderr with `-o json`, so stdout holds only the JSON document (decision D1).
- `[warning]`, `[error]`, `[debug]`, hint lines and progress go to stderr.
- Stdout data (`true`/`false`, `-o json`, `cluster map`, tables, one-time passwords) is never colored. A one-time password is printed unredacted exactly once, after a `[warning]`.
- Quiet (`-q`, `CBCTL_QUIET`) hides `[ok]`, `[info]`, `[debug]` and progress. Warnings, errors and data stay.

## Color decision (per stream, `output.Decider.Color`)

1. `--color never` off, `--color always` on.
2. `NO_COLOR` non-empty: off.
3. `TERM=dumb`: off.
4. `CLICOLOR_FORCE` or `FORCE_COLOR` non-empty and not `0`: on (`FORCE_COLOR=0`: off).
5. `CLICOLOR=0`: off.
6. Otherwise on only if that stream is a terminal.

Stdout and stderr are decided independently. Never reimplement terminal checks; use `output.Decider` (tests inject `Deps.IsTerminal`).

## Glyphs

`glyphPolicy` in `internal/cli/output.go` is `output.GlyphsByColor`: a stream that gets color shows `→ · ± … ••••`; every other stream shows ASCII `-> - +/- ... ****`. Write the Unicode spelling in source; `Glyphs.Localize` rewrites it per stream in `writeLabeled`, `writeProse`, `writePrompt`, the `Renderer` and the plan renderer. Code that builds text for a known stream (`plan.RenderPlanText`, `ActionLines`) takes an `output.Glyphs` argument from `outGlyphs(w)` / `stdoutGlyphs()`. `redact.MaskTail(s, mask)` gets its mask from the caller; it reads no global terminal state. `--version` licence text is the one fixed Unicode string.

## Rules to enforce

- Redact first (`redact.String`), then add escape codes, so a secret is never split by SGR codes.
- Tests assert exact bytes for color on and off; regenerate `internal/output` goldens with `go test ./internal/output -update` and review the diff. Command-level goldens live in `internal/cli/testdata/output`; regenerate with `go test ./internal/cli -run TestCommandOutputGolden -update-output`.
- Tests that match output text use the ASCII spelling (`->`, `-`), because tests run without a color terminal. Fake a terminal with `Deps.IsTerminal` to test the Unicode spelling.
- README color section and `.cursor/rules/cbctl.mdc` change in the same commit as any user-visible output change.
